# Backend environment variables — copy to .env for local use. NEVER commit .env.
#
# CREATORAI_SECRET  (REQUIRED in production) Strong random string used to sign
#                   JWT auth tokens. The app warns if you leave the dev default.
#                   Generate one:  python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(48))"
#
# CORS_ORIGINS      Comma-separated origins allowed to call the API (your Vercel
#                   URL in production). Localhost origins are always allowed.
#                   Example: CORS_ORIGINS=https://your-app.vercel.app
#
# CREATORAI_DB      Path to the SQLite database file. On Render this is /data/creatorai.db.
#                   Leave unset locally to use ./creatorai.db.
#
# CREATORAI_UPLOADS Directory for uploaded deliverable files. On Render: /data/uploads.
#
# DATABASE_URL      (Optional) If set to a Postgres URL, the app uses Postgres instead of
#                   SQLite. Leave unset to keep using SQLite on the persistent disk.
#
# LLM_API_URL       (Optional) External LLM endpoint used for brief generation, if any.
